# Cloudflare Pages types a file by its extension, and the four routes below are
# the only files in the build that do not have one: Next names a metadata image
# after its route, so they are written as `out/icon` and `out/opengraph-image`.
# Untyped they go out as application/octet-stream, which is a favicon a browser
# will not draw and a card no scraper will open.
#
# Nothing else needs a line here. Every other file in `out/` is a `.html`, a
# `.png`, a `.txt` or a `.xml` and says so in its name.
#
# `:slug` matches one path segment, which is the shape of the post cards. A
# splat would be the wrong tool: it is greedy, and `/blog/*` is the blog itself.

/icon
  Content-Type: image/png

/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png

/blog/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png

/blog/:slug/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
